---
import Illustration from './home/Illustration.astro';
import Adopters from './home/Adopters.astro';
import Ecosystem from './home/Ecosystem.astro';
import Issuance from './home/Issuance.astro';
import { latestSpireRelease } from '../../scripts/markdown.mjs';
import '../styles/homepage.css';

const release = latestSpireRelease();
const concepts = '/docs/latest/spiffe-about/spiffe-concepts/';
---
<div class="homepage not-content" data-pagefind-body>
  <section class="hp-hero hp-wrap" aria-labelledby="_top">
    <div class="hp-hero-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="hp-eyebrow"><span class="hp-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> An open standard</p>
        <h1 id="_top">Workload identity<br /> with <span>SPIFFE.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="hp-hero-copy">
        <p class="hp-lead">Give software a verifiable identity, wherever it runs.</p>
        <p>SPIFFE defines how workloads identify themselves and how other systems verify that identity. SPIRE is an open-source implementation.</p>
        <div class="hp-actions">
          <a class="hp-primary" href={concepts}>Understand SPIFFE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="hp-text-link" href="/docs/latest/spire-about/">Run SPIRE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hp-hero-figure">
      <Illustration variant="hero" />
      <figcaption>
        <p>Software can prove who it is.<br />The receiving service decides what it can do.</p>
        <ul class="hp-environments" aria-label="Example environments"><li>Kubernetes</li><li>Virtual machines</li><li>Datacenters</li><li>Edge</li></ul>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <div class="hp-wrap"><Adopters /></div>

  <section class="hp-foundation hp-wrap" aria-label="The identity model">
    <div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Workload authentication</p><h2 id="workload-authentication">How does a service know who is calling?</h2><p>When a workload makes a request, the receiving service needs to establish its identity. An IP address or hostname alone does not authenticate the caller. Passwords and API keys copied into deployments must be distributed and replaced wherever they are used.</p></div>
    <div><p class="hp-eyebrow">The model</p><h2 id="identity-model">SPIFFE IDs and SVIDs</h2><p>A SPIFFE ID names a workload within a trust domain. An SVID provides verifiable evidence of that identity. Applications can obtain SVIDs and trust bundles through the SPIFFE Workload API.</p></div>
    <div><p class="hp-eyebrow">The result</p><h2 id="access-decisions">Authentication between services</h2><p>Services verify the identity presented by a caller and use it in their access decisions. Operators choose how SPIFFE IDs map to their workloads and environments.</p></div>
  </section>

  <Issuance />

  <section class="hp-concepts hp-wrap hp-section" aria-labelledby="concepts-heading">
    <div class="hp-section-heading"><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Concepts</p><h2 id="concepts-heading">SPIFFE concepts</h2></div><a class="hp-text-link" href={concepts}>Read the concepts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <dl class="hp-concept-grid">
      <div><dt><a href={concepts + '#spiffe-id'}>SPIFFE ID <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dt><dd>A URI that names a workload within a trust domain.<code>spiffe://example.org/orders</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href={concepts + '#spiffe-verifiable-identity-document-svid'}>SVID <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dt><dd>A verifiable identity document that binds a SPIFFE ID to a key or token.<code>X.509-SVID · JWT-SVID</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href={concepts + '#spiffe-workload-api'}>Workload API <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dt><dd>A local interface for obtaining SVIDs and trust bundles.<code>FetchX509SVID<br />FetchJWTSVID</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href={concepts + '#trust-domain'}>Trust domain <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dt><dd>An administrative boundary with its own issuing authority.<code>example.org</code></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="hp-applications hp-wrap hp-section" aria-labelledby="applications-heading">
    <div class="hp-section-heading"><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Applications</p><h2 id="applications-heading">Workload authentication</h2></div><p>Services, jobs and agents can use SPIFFE credentials to authenticate to other software.</p></div>
    <div class="hp-application-grid">
      <article><Illustration variant="services" /><p class="hp-eyebrow">01 / Services</p><h3>Authentication between services</h3><p>Use X.509-SVIDs for mutual TLS, or audience-scoped JWT-SVIDs to authenticate HTTP and gRPC requests. The receiving service verifies the credential and applies its access policy.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href={concepts + '#spiffe-verifiable-identity-document-svid'}>SPIFFE credentials <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article><Illustration variant="platforms" /><p class="hp-eyebrow">02 / Platforms</p><h3>Authentication to platforms</h3><p>Present an SVID to a compatible service, or exchange it for platform credentials with a scoped lifetime.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href="/docs/latest/spiffe-about/ecosystem/">Explore integrations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article><Illustration variant="federation" /><p class="hp-eyebrow">03 / Federation</p><h3>Work across trust domains.</h3><p>Independently operated domains exchange public trust bundles so they can verify each other’s identities. Each service retains its own access policy.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href="/docs/latest/architecture/federation/readme/">Federation with SPIRE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hp-projects hp-wrap hp-section" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
    <div class="hp-section-heading"><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Companion projects</p><h2 id="projects-heading">SPIFFE and SPIRE.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="hp-project-grid">
      <article class="hp-standard"><img src="/img/logos/spiffe/horizontal/color/spiffe-horizontal-color.svg" alt="SPIFFE" width="154" height="52" loading="lazy" /><p class="hp-eyebrow">Open standard</p><h3>The workload identity standard.</h3><p>SPIFFE defines how identities are named and represented, how workloads obtain them, and how trust domains interoperate.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href="/docs/latest/spiffe-specs/">Read the specifications <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article class="hp-implementation"><img src="/img/logos/spire/horizontal/color/spire-horizontal-color.svg" alt="SPIRE" width="154" height="52" loading="lazy" /><p class="hp-eyebrow">Open-source implementation</p><h3>Workload identity with SPIRE</h3><p>SPIRE is a CNCF graduated project that implements the SPIFFE standard. It uses node and workload attestation to issue short-lived identity credentials and keep them current. Plugins adapt attestation to your environment and connect SPIRE to existing certificate authorities and key-management systems.</p><div class="hp-actions"><a class="hp-text-link" href="/docs/latest/spire-about/">Explore SPIRE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="hp-text-link" href="/downloads/">{release.tag_name ? `Get SPIRE ${release.tag_name}` : 'Get SPIRE'} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Ecosystem />

  <section class="hp-resources hp-wrap hp-section" aria-labelledby="resources-heading">
    <div class="hp-section-heading"><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Resources</p><h2 id="resources-heading">Learn about SPIFFE</h2></div></div>
    <div class="hp-resource-grid">
      <a class="hp-resource hp-video" aria-labelledby="resource-intro" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q2SiGeebRKY"><div class="hp-resource-art" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 230 135"><path d="M47 31Q47 21 57 21H181Q191 21 191 31V104Q191 114 181 114H57Q47 114 47 104Z" fill="#beda00"/><rect x="39" y="13" width="144" height="93" rx="12" fill="white" stroke="#1f2a2e" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="111" cy="60" r="22" fill="#00beda"/><path d="M106 49L122 60L106 71Z" fill="white"/></svg></div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Watch / 10 minutes</p><h3 id="resource-intro">Introduction to SPIFFE.</h3><p>The problem, the identity model, and where SPIRE fits.</p><span class="hp-text-link">Watch the introduction ↗</span></a>
      <a class="hp-resource hp-book" aria-labelledby="resource-book" href="/book/"><div class="hp-resource-art"><img src="/img/book_cover.png" alt="Solving the Bottom Turtle book cover" width="100" height="135" loading="lazy" /></div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Read / The SPIFFE book</p><h3 id="resource-book">Solving the Bottom Turtle.</h3><p>Designing and operating workload identity in distributed systems.</p><span class="hp-text-link">Read the book ↗</span></a>
      <a class="hp-resource hp-community" aria-labelledby="resource-community" href="/docs/latest/spiffe-about/get-involved/"><div class="hp-resource-art" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 230 135"><circle cx="115" cy="66" r="51" fill="#00beda"/><path d="M53 33H148Q158 33 158 43V78Q158 88 148 88H85L62 105V88H53Q43 88 43 78V43Q43 33 53 33Z" fill="white" stroke="#1f2a2e" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M63 52H138M63 66H113" stroke="#00beda" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M168 57H179Q188 57 188 66V94Q188 103 179 103H165L149 116V103H125Q117 103 117 96" fill="none" stroke="#1f2a2e" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Participate / Community</p><h3 id="resource-community">SPIFFE community</h3><p>Meetings, discussions, and contribution guidelines.</p><span class="hp-text-link">Get involved ↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="hp-training"><h3>Training and labs</h3><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Linux Foundation / LFS183</p><h4>Introduction to Zero Trust</h4><p>Explore workload identity through exercises in PKI, mutual TLS, SPIRE, and policy enforcement with OPA and Envoy.</p><div class="hp-actions"><a class="hp-text-link" href="https://trainingportal.linuxfoundation.org/courses/introduction-to-zero-trust-lfs183">Course page ↗</a><a class="hp-text-link" href="https://github.com/lftraining/LFS183x-resources">Labs ↗</a></div></div><div><p class="hp-eyebrow">Linux Foundation / LFS482</p><h4>SPIFFE and SPIRE labs</h4><p>Deploy SPIRE, obtain workload credentials, and configure federation. Continue with high availability and integrations with OPA, Envoy, and Cilium.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href="https://github.com/lftraining/lfs482-labs">Explore the labs ↗</a></div></div>
  </section>

  <div class="hp-cncf hp-wrap"><img src="/img/logos/cncf-color.png" alt="Cloud Native Computing Foundation" width="174" height="64" loading="lazy" /><p>SPIFFE and SPIRE are CNCF graduated projects.</p><a class="hp-text-link" href="https://www.cncf.io/projects/spiffe/">Project information ↗</a></div>
  <img class="hp-telemetry" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://static.scarf.sh/a.png?x-pxid=360e600b-8ddf-4aad-92e7-76c93e550e8f" alt="" width="1" height="1" />
</div>
